Option A: Caddy (Empfohlen - automatische SSL-Zertifikate) /etc/caddy/Caddyfile: wissen-ahrensburg.de { reverse_proxy localhost:5000
} doc.wissen-ahrensburg.de { reverse_proxy localhost:5000
} Option B: Nginx /etc/nginx/sites-available/meincms: server { server_name wissen-ahrensburg.de doc.wissen-ahrensburg.de; location / { proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:5000; proxy_set_header Host $host; proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr; proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for; proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme; }
